# Core Engine

Map of this area: `docs/architecture/engine.md` (engine), `game.md` (reducer), `data.md` (stats).

- Pure and deterministic: same input and same seed produce the same output.
- Randomness only through the injected `Rng` (`createRng(seed)`); time only through arguments (`now`).
- State is immutable: reducers return new objects. Mutable internals (typed arrays, scratch lines) are
  allowed inside a function for performance but never escape it.
- A grid is a flat row-major array of length `rows * cols`. Use the helpers in `engine/grid.ts`
  (`indexOf`, `rowCells`, `colCells`, `lineCells`) instead of recomputing indices.
- Line deductions work on `Line` arrays of `LineCell` (`unknown | filled | crossed`) and never read
  the solution.

```ts
// BAD
for (let i = 0; i < rows * cols; i++) if (Math.floor(i / cols) === row) ...
// GOOD
for (const i of rowCells(size, row)) ...
```

- Every public function has tests next to it.
- Changing generator output requires bumping `GENERATOR_VERSION`; changing the analyzer requires
  bumping `ANALYZER_VERSION` (both in `engine/versions.ts`) and rebuilding packs (`pnpm build:packs`).
- Keep `core` alias-free (relative imports) so Node scripts can import it.
